    "result_text": "Green. The change is complete.\n\n## What I did\n\nAdded an email-uniqueness rule to `POST /api/owners`, mirroring the existing telephone/household uniqueness pattern so the logic lands where it belongs rather than being folded into an existing step:\n\n1. **`EnsureUniqueEmail`** (function) \u2014 runs after `NormalizeOwnerEmail` has lower-cased the body's email, then rejects the request if that value equals any existing owner's email (compared in the same lower-cased form via the shared `Emails.normalize`). A blank/absent email carries no identity, so it's skipped.\n2. **`DuplicateEmailException`** \u2014 checked exception carrying the offending email, so it appears in the `throws` clause and routes to an escalation.\n3. **`DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler`** + its escalation YAML \u2014 responds **409 Conflict** with a `ProblemDetail`, exactly like the telephone handler.\n4. Wired `ensureUniqueEmail` into `owners.POST.yml` alongside the other uniqueness checks (after `ensureUniqueTelephone`, under the same `transaction` governance).\n\nI reused `Emails.normalize` and `OwnerRepository.findAll()` rather than duplicating normalization or query logic. The new `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
